    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Build
        run: |
          xcodebuild build -scheme MyApp \
            -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' \
            -derivedDataPath build/
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: app-binary
          path: build/Build/Products/Debug-iphonesimulator/MyApp.app

  visual-regression:
    needs: build
    runs-on: macos-15
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: app-binary
          path: ./app
      - name: Install Grantiva CLI
        run: brew install grantiva/tap/grantiva
      - name: Visual regression
        env:
          GRANTIVA_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.GRANTIVA_API_KEY }}
        run: |
          grantiva ci run --app-file ./app/MyApp.app
```

Results upload to the [Grantiva](https://grantiva.io) dashboard and post as GitHub Check Runs on your PRs.

## Commands

OVERVIEW: The Grantiva CLI for iOS and Android developers.

USAGE: grantiva <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  build                   Build and optionally install the app to a simulator
                          or emulator.
  run                     Run Maestro flows against a simulator or emulator. No
                          visual regression — reports step pass/fail and
                          captures a screenshot on failure.
  record                  Record a simulator or emulator and extract PNG frames
                          at exact requested timestamps.
  simulator               Provision, inspect, and tear down managed simulators.
  emulator                Provision, inspect, and tear down Android emulators.
  hierarchy               Dump the UI hierarchy of a booted simulator or
                          emulator without relaunching the app.
  ci                      CI pipeline — capture, compare, and upload results.
  diff                    Visual regression testing — capture, compare, and
                          approve screenshots.
  auth                    Manage authentication with Grantiva.
  console                 Manage your Grantiva dashboard from the terminal.
  doctor                  Check environment and dependencies.
  runner                  Manage the embedded UI automation runner.
  init                    Generate grantiva.yml (iOS) or grantiva-android.yml
                          (Android) in the current directory.
  mcp                     Start the Grantiva MCP server for AI agent
                          integration.

  See 'grantiva help <subcommand>' for detailed help.
OVERVIEW: Run Maestro flows against a simulator or emulator. No visual
regression — reports step pass/fail and captures a screenshot on failure.

USAGE: grantiva run <options>

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --app-file <app-file>   Path to a pre-built app: .app bundle or .ipa archive
                          (iOS), .apk (Android). Skips the build step.
  --no-build              Skip building and installing — assume the app is
                          already on the device. With --app-file, that file is
                          installed (only the build is skipped).
  --derived-data-path <derived-data-path>
                          Write Xcode build products and intermediates to this
                          DerivedData directory.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --scheme <scheme>       Scheme to build (iOS)
  --simulator <simulator> Simulator name or UDID (iOS)
  --bundle-id <bundle-id> Bundle identifier (iOS)
  --module <module>       Gradle module to assemble (Android; default app)
  --variant <variant>     Gradle build variant, e.g. debug or freeDebug
                          (Android; default debug)
  --application-id <application-id>
                          Application ID (Android; read from the build or the
                          APK when omitted)
  --emulator <emulator>   AVD name to use, booting it if needed (Android)
  --device <device>       adb serial of an attached emulator or physical device
                          (Android); for a build, its ABI picks the split APK
  --allow-device-settings Apply demo mode and animation settings on a physical
                          device too (Android)
  --headless              Boot an emulator without a window (Android).
                          GRANTIVA_EMULATOR_HEADLESS=1 or CI=true does the
                          same; otherwise a booted emulator gets a window, even
                          when stdout is not a terminal.
  --flow <flow>           Run a single flow file instead of all configured flows
  --keep-alive            Keep the runner session (GrantivaAgent on iOS,
                          UIAutomator2 on Android) alive after flows complete
                          so `grantiva hierarchy` can inspect UI state without
                          relaunching the app. Release with Ctrl-C.
  --logs                  Stream app logs from the simulator or emulator into
                          this terminal, prefixed with [log] (iOS and Android).
                          On iOS the filter defaults to lines whose subsystem
                          starts with the app's bundle ID or whose process is
                          the app's executable; on Android, to lines from the
                          app's uid.
  --logs-predicate <logs-predicate>
                          Custom NSPredicate for `simctl log stream
                          --predicate` (iOS). Implies --logs.
  --logs-tag <logs-tag>   logcat tag to keep when streaming logs (Android).
                          Implies --logs.
  --logs-level <logs-level>
                          Log level for --logs: default, info, debug. Defaults
                          to `default`. iOS passes it to `log stream --level`;
                          on Android default and info keep logcat priority I
                          and above, debug adds D. (values: default, info,
                          debug)
  --snapshot <snapshot>   Snapshot policy: failure (default — one shot after
                          failure), trailing (last-good step + failure step),
                          full (every step). (values: failure, trailing, full;
                          default: failure)
  --continue-on-failure   Keep running remaining flows after a failure. Default
                          is fail-fast — stop the suite on the first broken
                          flow, which matches CI semantics and avoids wasting
                          cycles.
  --report-dir <report-dir>
                          Write the runner's report.json + assets to this
                          directory (workspace-relative). Survives grantiva's
                          cleanup so CI can upload it. Default: ephemeral tmp
                          dir.
  --timeout <timeout>     Max seconds to wait for the runner subprocess before
                          killing it with SIGTERM. Default: 600 (10 min).
                          Minimum 30. Ignored under --keep-alive. Bump this for
                          long multi-flow suites. (default: 600)
  --ready-file <ready-file>
                          Write this file once the run reaches a terminal
                          state, containing its status. Deleted at startup, and
                          always written — a setup failure records `failed`
                          rather than leaving a waiter hanging. Missing parent
                          directories are created. Wait on it with `while [ !
                          -f <path> ]; do sleep 0.2; done` instead of polling
                          report.json — useful with --keep-alive, where the
                          session outlives the flows.
  --env <env>             Environment variable for the app under test, as
                          KEY=VALUE. Repeatable. Forwarded through the flow's
                          launchApp (environment on iOS, string intent extras
                          on Android).
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Build and optionally install the app to a simulator or emulator.

USAGE: grantiva build <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  build (default)         Build the app for a simulator (xcodebuild) or
                          emulator (Gradle).
  install                 Build and install the app on a simulator or emulator,
                          then optionally launch it.

  See 'grantiva help build <subcommand>' for detailed help.
OVERVIEW: Record a simulator or emulator and extract PNG frames at exact
requested timestamps.

USAGE: grantiva record [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--platform <platform>] [--simulator <simulator>] [--emulator <emulator>] [--device <device>] --duration <duration> [--output <output>] [--frames-at <frames-at>]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --simulator <simulator> Simulator name or UDID to record (iOS; reads
                          simulator from grantiva.yml if omitted)
  --emulator <emulator>   AVD name to record, booting it if needed (Android;
                          reads emulator from grantiva-android.yml if omitted)
  --device <device>       adb serial of an attached emulator or device (Android)
  --duration <duration>   Recording duration in seconds (Android caps a
                          recording at 180)
  --output <output>       Output video path. Must end in .mov on iOS and .mp4
                          on Android, the containers each platform records
                          (default: .grantiva/recordings/recording.mov on iOS,
                          .mp4 on Android)
  --frames-at <frames-at> Comma-separated frame timestamps in milliseconds,
                          e.g. 0,150,300,600
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Dump the UI hierarchy of a booted simulator or emulator without
relaunching the app.

Finds the session published by `grantiva run --keep-alive` (in
/tmp/grantiva-sessions, with the simulator UDID or adb serial recorded by
grantiva) and reads the current page source: from GrantivaAgent on iOS, from
the UIAutomator2 server on Android. The target app is never touched — no
launch, no stopApp, no clearState.

Typical agent workflow:

    # Terminal 1 (or backgrounded in CI):
    grantiva run --keep-alive --flow flows/onboarding.yaml

    # Terminal 2:
    grantiva hierarchy > state.xml

If no keep-alive session is running, this command fails with a clear message
rather than trying to start one (which would relaunch the app and destroy the
state you wanted to inspect).

USAGE: grantiva hierarchy [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--udid <udid>] [--timeout <timeout>] [--format <format>]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --udid <udid>           Simulator UDID or adb serial to target (default:
                          newest keep-alive session)
  --timeout <timeout>     Seconds to wait for GrantivaAgent's (iOS) or
                          UIAutomator2's (Android) page-source response.
                          Default: 60. (default: 60.0)
  --format <format>       Output format: xml (default) or json. --json is the
                          same as --format json. (values: xml, json)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Check environment and dependencies.

USAGE: grantiva doctor [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--platform <platform>]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Generate grantiva.yml (iOS) or grantiva-android.yml (Android) in the
current directory.

USAGE: grantiva init [--verbose] [--quiet] [--platform <platform>] [--scheme <scheme>] [--bundle-id <bundle-id>] [--application-id <application-id>]

OPTIONS:
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --scheme <scheme>       Scheme name
  --bundle-id <bundle-id> Bundle identifier
  --application-id <application-id>
                          Application ID (Android)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Start the Grantiva MCP server for AI agent integration.

The server starts without a runner session or a config file. Device tools
(grantiva_tap, grantiva_swipe, grantiva_type, grantiva_screenshot,
grantiva_a11y_*, grantiva_script) need a runner session and return an error
until one exists (while one is starting, an error saying so and to retry in a
few seconds); they pick it up on the next call. The session is the project's
.grantiva/session.json (grantiva runner start), or a grantiva run --keep-alive
or runner start session started from the same project directory for the same
platform. Sessions from other projects or the other platform are never used.
Simulator, emulator, build, context, and VRT tools work without a session.

USAGE: grantiva mcp [--project-dir <project-dir>] [--platform <platform>]

OPTIONS:
  --project-dir <project-dir>
                          Project directory (default: the current directory).
                          Its grantiva.yml or grantiva-android.yml and runner
                          session are used when present.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

